<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Korea and Japan</p><h1 class="st-title">Satake clan domain</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1602 CE (approx.) · capital Ota, later Mito</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The domain of the Satake of Hitachi, an old warrior house that dominated northeastern Kanto in the Sengoku period before its transfer to Akita in 1602.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Satake, a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seiwa-genji">Seiwa Genji</a>, had been established in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hitachi-province">Hitachi</a> since the 12th century. After long internal conflicts, they restored their unity around 1500 and from their castle at Ota expanded across the province.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satake-yoshishige">Satake Yoshishige</a>, nicknamed the demon of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hitachi-province">Hitachi</a>, fought the Later Hojo for control of the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanto-region">Kanto</a> and allied with neighbours to resist them. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satake-yoshinobu">Yoshinobu</a> supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a>, joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-odawara-1590">siege of Odawara</a> in 1590, and was confirmed in a large fief across Hitachi, moving his seat to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mito-ibaraki">Mito</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satake-yoshinobu">Yoshinobu</a> remained neutral at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara">Sekigahara</a> in 1600, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> punished him in 1602 by transferring the clan to the much smaller <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kubota-domain">Kubota Domain</a> in Dewa, where the Satake ruled until 1871.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/satake-clan-domain.jpg" alt="Satake clan domain" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: Mukai · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Japanese_Crest_Hinomaru_Oogi.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 CE – 1602 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ota, later Mito</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Satake Yoshishige, Satake Yoshinobu</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Middle Japanese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Japan</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Satake clan, Satake of Hitachi</dd></dl></aside></div>
